<title>POLAND: BIG cleared to buy 50 pct Gdanski.</title>
<headline>BIG cleared to buy 50 pct Gdanski.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish bank BIG SA has received the permission of the National Bank of Poland (NBP), the central bank, to hold between 50 and 66 percent of Bank Gdanski, BIG said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>BIG, whose full name is Bank Inicjatyw Gospodarczych SA, currently has 31.23 percent of Gdanski shares directly and through two of its subsidiaries, and is the only bidder for the treasury's offer of another 31.9 percent stake, or 6,260,240 shares, in Gdanski.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
